        <definition>SgAsmExpression* SgAsmMemoryReferenceExpression::segment</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>segment</name>
        <initializer>= <ref refid="ModuleBuilder_8h_1ab979d9d4b4923f7c54d6caa6e1a61936" kindref="member">nullptr</ref></initializer>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Property: Optional memory segment register.</para><para>If a segment register is specified then the actual memory address is formed by adding the stored memory address to the current value of the segment register. The x86 architecture is the only ROSE architecture that uses segment registers, and most of the time they are initialized to zero by the instruction semantics. </para>        </detaileddescription>
